            <ArticleTitle>Draft Genome Sequence of Pseudomonas aeruginosa ATCC 9027, Originally Isolated from an Outer Ear Infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e01397-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.01397-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pseudomonas aeruginosa ATCC 9027 was isolated in 1943 from a case of otitis externa and is commonly employed as a quality control strain for sterility, assessment of antibiofilm agents, and in vitro study of wound infection. Here, we present the 6.34-Mb draft genome sequence and highlight some pertinent genes that are associated with virulence.</AbstractText>
